            <ArticleTitle>Beta agonist use during asthma exacerbations: how much is too much?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Overuse of inhaled beta agonist therapy is associated with risk in adult asthmatics. We report on a case of excessive short-acting and long-acting beta agonist use in the setting of a severe exacerbation of asthma, which highlights some important good practice points.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
